From: Joel Wiramu Pauling <aenertia@aenertia.net>
Date: Wed, 02 Apr 2026 12:00:00 +1300
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: Add XDP, TCP LRO, and hybrid QoS support

Add XDP (eXpress Data Path) support for the Airoha AN7581 ethernet driver,
enabling high-performance packet processing with eBPF programs. Also adds
TCP hardware Large Receive Offload (LRO) for 8 hw queues (0-7).

Ported from 6.12 to 6.18 kernel:
- TX path rewritten for linked-list descriptor model (v6.19 patch 108)
- RX cleanup reconciled with upstream patch 135 (desc field resets)
- airoha_qdma_cleanup() uses new signature from patch 133

Phase 2 additions (ADR-001):
- Copy XDP metadata marks (0xAF01..04) to skb->mark for nft/tc visibility
- Derive skb->priority from IP DSCP for hardware queue selection
- Populate FOE entry CHANNEL/QID/IB2_DSCP from flow DSCP for ETS scheduling
- DSCP-to-queue mapping: bulk->ch0, normal->ch1, interactive->ch2, rt->ch3

XDP features:
- XDP_PASS, XDP_TX, XDP_REDIRECT, XDP_DROP actions
- ndo_bpf and ndo_xdp_xmit callbacks
- Uses linked-list TX descriptor allocation (6.18 model)

LRO features (from Lorenzo Bianconi's patches):
- airoha_qdma_rx_queue_deinit utility routine
- airoha_qdma_init_rx_pp routine with LRO-aware page pool sizing
- Full TCP LRO with ndo_set_features toggle support

Signed-off-by: Joel Wiramu Pauling <aenertia@aenertia.net>
Co-developed-by: Lorenzo Bianconi <lorenzo@kernel.org>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c	2026-04-03 16:13:52.544276500 +1300
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c	2026-04-03 16:13:52.549223854 +1300
@@ -493,6 +493,39 @@
 		airoha_fe_clear(eth, REG_CDM_LRO_RXQ(id, i), LRO_RXQ_MASK(i));
 }
 
+static void airoha_fe_lro_init_rx_queue(struct airoha_eth *eth, int id,
+					int lro_queue_index, int qid,
+					int nbuf, int buf_size)
+{
+	airoha_fe_rmw(eth, REG_CDM_LRO_LIMIT(id),
+		      CDM_LRO_AGG_NUM_MASK | CDM_LRO_AGG_SIZE_MASK,
+		      FIELD_PREP(CDM_LRO_AGG_NUM_MASK, nbuf) |
+		      FIELD_PREP(CDM_LRO_AGG_SIZE_MASK, buf_size));
+	airoha_fe_rmw(eth, REG_CDM_LRO_AGE_TIME(id),
+		      CDM_LRO_AGE_TIME_MASK | CDM_LRO_AGG_TIME_MASK,
+		      FIELD_PREP(CDM_LRO_AGE_TIME_MASK,
+				 AIROHA_RXQ_LRO_MAX_AGE_TIME) |
+		      FIELD_PREP(CDM_LRO_AGG_TIME_MASK,
+				 AIROHA_RXQ_LRO_MAX_AGG_TIME));
+	airoha_fe_rmw(eth, REG_CDM_LRO_RXQ(id, lro_queue_index),
+		      LRO_RXQ_MASK(lro_queue_index),
+		      qid << __ffs(LRO_RXQ_MASK(lro_queue_index)));
+	airoha_fe_set(eth, REG_CDM_LRO_EN(id), BIT(lro_queue_index));
+}
+
+static void airoha_fe_lro_disable(struct airoha_eth *eth, int id)
+{
+	int i;
+
+	airoha_fe_clear(eth, REG_CDM_LRO_LIMIT(id),
+			CDM_LRO_AGG_NUM_MASK | CDM_LRO_AGG_SIZE_MASK);
+	airoha_fe_clear(eth, REG_CDM_LRO_AGE_TIME(id),
+			CDM_LRO_AGE_TIME_MASK | CDM_LRO_AGG_TIME_MASK);
+	airoha_fe_clear(eth, REG_CDM_LRO_EN(id), LRO_RXQ_EN_MASK);
+	for (i = 0; i < AIROHA_MAX_NUM_LRO_QUEUES; i++)
+		airoha_fe_clear(eth, REG_CDM_LRO_RXQ(id, i), LRO_RXQ_MASK(i));
+}
